The 4th Commandment:


Honor your father and your mother!


God gave this commandment to mankind. But it has caused unspeakable spiritual struggles. Many a child and many an adult have struggled hard not to violate this commandment in the most blatant way.


How can a child honor a father who has degraded himself to the level of a drunkard, or a mother who, through her moods, her unbridled temper, her lack of self-discipline, and so many other things, makes the hours of her father and the whole house so bitter that it is impossible for her to have a peaceful atmosphere!


Can a child honor his parents when he hears that they insult each other harshly, betray each other, or even hit each other? Many marital events often made the commandment a torment for the children, making it impossible to fulfill it.


After all, it would be hypocrisy if a child were to claim to still honor a mother when she behaves much more kindly towards strangers than towards her own husband, the child's father. If it notices her tendency towards superficiality, if it sees her sinking into the most ridiculous vanity into a mindless slave to every fashionable folly, which so often can no longer be reconciled with the concept of serious, noble motherhood, which robs all the beauty and sublimity of motherhood, ... how can a child then still find voluntary reverence for the mother? What is there in the one word: "mother"! But what does it ask for?


A child who has not yet been poisoned must unconsciously feel within himself that a person with a mature, serious mind will never be able to decide to expose his physical body merely for the sake of fashion. How can the mother then remain sacred to the child! Natural reverence sinks impulsively into the empty form of a habitual obligation or, depending on the upbringing, into the self-evident social politeness, i.e. into hypocrisy, which lacks any spiritual exaltation. It is precisely the exaltation that contains warm life within itself, which is indispensable to a child and accompanies it like a safe shield as it grows up and steps out into life, protects it from all kinds of temptations, and which remains a strong inner refuge for it when it has any doubts. Right into old age!


The word "mother" or "father" should always evoke a warm, heartfelt feeling, from which the image in its full purity stands before the soul, warning or approving, as a guiding star in all earthly existence!


And what a treasure is taken from every child if he or she cannot honor his or her father or mother with all his or her soul !


But the reason for this mental anguish is again only the wrong understanding of the commandment on the part of man. The previous view was wrong, which limited the meaning and made it one-sided, while nothing that God has sent can be one-sided.


But it was even more incorrect that this commandment was distorted by trying to improve it according to human judgment, making it even more specific by adding: "Honor your father and your mother!" This made it personal. This was bound to lead to errors, because the commandment in its correct form only says: "Honor your father and your mother!"


It does not refer to specific individuals whose nature cannot be determined or predicted in advance . Such absurdities never occur in divine laws. God does not demand that we honor something that does not absolutely deserve to be honored!


On the contrary, this commandment encompasses a concept of fatherhood and motherhood rather than personality . It is therefore not addressed to the children first, but to the parents themselves, and demands that they uphold fatherhood and motherhood! The commandment imposes unconditional duties on parents to always be fully aware of their high task and thus also to keep in mind the responsibility that lies with it.


In the afterlife and in the light one does not live with words, but in concepts.


For this reason, when these terms are translated into the Word, a restriction of these concepts can easily occur, as is evident in this case. But woe to those who do not respect this commandment, who do not endeavor to understand it correctly. It is no excuse that it has so often been misinterpreted and misunderstood.


The consequences of not obeying the commandment were already apparent at the time of conception and the entry of the soul. Things would be very different on this earth if people had understood and fulfilled the decisive commandment. Completely different souls could then incarnate, and it would not be possible for them to allow a decline in morality and ethics to the extent that it is today!


Just look at the murders, the wild dances, the orgies that everything is trying to escalate into today. As if it were the crowning glory of the triumph of the sultry currents of darkness. And look at the incomprehensible indifference with which people accept and even encourage the decline as something right or something that has always been there.


Where is the man who strives to understand the will of God correctly, who seeks to soar to grasp the infinite greatness, instead of stubbornly forcing this great will again and again into the miserable limitations of the earthly brain, which he has made the temple of the intellect? He thereby presses his own gaze to the ground like a slave who walks in chains, instead of raising it upwards with joyful radiance to meet the ray of knowledge.


Don't you see how poor you are in every understanding of everything that comes to you from the light! Be it commandments, the promises, the message of Christ or even the whole of creation! You don't want to see anything, you don't want to recognize anything! You don't even try to really understand anything! You don't take it as it is, but rather you try desperately to transform everything into the lower views to which you have surrendered for thousands of years.


Free yourselves at last from these traditions. The strength to do so is at your disposal. At any moment, and without you having to make any sacrifices. But it must be thrown away from you with a jolt, with an act of will! Without flirting with any of it. As soon as you try to find a transition , you will never be free of what has gone before, but it will always stubbornly pull you back. It can only be easy for you if you separate everything old with one cut and thus step into the new without the old burden. Only then will the gate open for you, otherwise it will remain firmly closed.


And that only requires a really serious desire, it is the happening of an instant. Just like waking up from sleep. If you don't get up from your bed right away, you will get tired again and the joy of the new day's work will wane, if it is not completely lost.


You shall honor your father and mother! This is now a holy commandment for you. Honor fatherhood and motherhood! Who knows today what great dignity lies in this? And what power to ennoble humanity! People who unite here on earth should be clear about this, then every marriage will really be a marriage, anchored in the spiritual! And all fathers and mothers will be honorable according to the divine laws!


But for children this commandment becomes holy and alive through their parents. They will have no choice but to honor their father and mother from the bottom of their hearts, no matter what the nature of these children themselves is. They will be compelled to do so by the nature of their parents.


And woe to those children who do not fully comply with the commandment. They would be burdened with heavy karma, because the reason for it would then be fully given. But following it will soon become a matter of course, a joy, a necessity! Therefore, go and take God's commandments more seriously than before! That means, observe and fulfill them! So that you will be happy!


